-- Divide-by-zero TRAP probe. The divisor is a clogger byte; fed a zero byte it
-- is a runtime division by zero. The native ELF must fault CLEANLY: exit 1,
-- empty stdout, NO SIGFPE/#DE crash (its back end guards with `test rcx,rcx;
-- jz <diag_div>` before `div`). link15 grades the status and the empty stdout.
-- Since K4 the program also prints `herbert: line 11: division by zero` on
-- stderr; link15 does not grade stderr (the conformance cases pin that text).
func main():
    let inp = clogger()
    let a = index(inp, 0)
    let b = index(inp, 1)
    return a / b
end
